# Dependency and Tooling Policy

- Use Bun/Bunx for scripts and package operations in this repo.
- Agents invoking Bun from a terminal must prefix it with `env`, as in `env bun run healthcheck`. Bun writes whatever `argv[0]` it receives into the `bun` and `node` symlinks it shares across the machine, and some editors launch shells that pass their own binary as `argv[0]`. Those scripts then silently run the editor and exit 0, so every check passes without running. `env` re-execs with a correct `argv[0]`. Drop this once Bun resolves the shim target from the executable path rather than `argv[0]`.
- Keep lint/format on Oxfmt and Oxlint; do not add ESLint/Prettier unless explicitly requested.
- Prefer per-repo dependencies over global installs.
- Do not add a new dependency without clear user benefit and justification.
- Prefer existing repo tooling and conventions before introducing alternatives.
- Keep lockfile and package manager usage consistent with the project standard.
- When changing tooling, update docs/scripts together to avoid drift.
